adaptation-samsung-beyond2lte (14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Deep sleep: hands-free auto-suspend daemon (s10-autosleep) with fast wake.
    The phone suspends (echo mem) when the graphical session is idle and no
    guard blocks (charger, audio, ssh, active transfer), and relights the
    screen on resume by feeding KEY_POWER into wayfire over its IPC (the power
    key is a wakeup source, so on a power-button wake it never reaches the
    compositor as "turn the screen on").
  * Deep sleep: the roughly 40 s blind screen after resume was wayfire closing
    every evdev fd on resume, each evdev_release calling synchronize_rcu; under
    preemptible non-expedited RCU one grace period took about 2 s, so about 20
    devices cost about 40 s. The daemon brackets the suspend with expedited RCU
    (rcu_expedited=1, rcu_normal=0) only for the suspend and resume, then
    restores the as-found state, so idle power is unchanged. Measured wake from
    about 40 s to 1.4 s (screen on at the first KEY_POWER inject).

 -- Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:45:00 +0200

adaptation-samsung-beyond2lte (13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rotation: wayfire plugin obrot in place of autorotate-iio. The last frame
    stays on the panel until every surface has redrawn at the new size (up to
    1 s, measured 364 to 476 ms), then fades into the live image, instead of
    half the screen showing old content and the rest black. The sensor is read
    in a GLib thread that wakes the compositor on a change, not once a second.

 -- Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 02:40:00 +0200

adaptation-samsung-beyond2lte (12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sound: accept ABOX firmware built into the kernel (boot image of
    03.10.2026, CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE); ABOX loads it without the user helper
    fallback, so serving /sys/class/firmware could never work.
  * Sound: wake ABOX once at android-mount, before the vendor HAL starts. The
    first runtime resume registers the firmware's ALSA controls under the
    card's controls_rwsem; triggered by the HAL reading a control it
    deadlocked (HAL in D state, pulseaudio hung).

 -- Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 01:45:00 +0200

